n law. Idaho's certification of trust requirement is notably stricter than UTC states — requiring an affidavit signed and acknowledged by ALL currently acting trustees, not just one. Idaho has no state estate or inheritance tax, making it attractive for trust situs.","provenance":{"sources":[{"label":"Idaho Code § 68-114","url":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/title68/t68ch1/sect68-114/","kind":"official"}],"verified_as_of":"2026-09-17","human_legal_reviewed":false,"evidence":"curl -> HTTP 200; page title '68-114 – Idaho State Legislature'; text 'TITLE 68 TRUSTS AND FIDUCIARIES CHAPTER 1 TRUSTS 68-114. Presentation of a certification of trust in lieu of the trust instrument — Effect — Form.'"}};
